  "img": "systems/draw-steel/assets/classes/conduit.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You are a working spellcaster of the classical elements - air, water, fire, earth - channeled through study, will, and a bonded focus rather than chrome or prayer. Corp records call you an \"environmental hazard specialist\" when they bother to admit you exist; the street calls you an <strong>Elementalist</strong>, or just points and gets out of the blast radius.</p><p>Your engine is <strong>Essence</strong>: a lean, always-flowing resource. Every turn you gain a free <strong>+1 Essence</strong> with no maneuver spent (the drip). You may also spend a maneuver to <strong>Channel</strong>, ramping your income to +2, then +3, then +4 on consecutive turns (switching your attuned element resets the ramp, not the drip). Landing an elemental hit grants +1 more the first time each round (resonance). You spend Essence on heroic abilities and to sustain ongoing workings (Persist 1 costs 2/turn, Persist 2 costs 4/turn). Unspent Essence is lost at the end of the encounter.</p><h3>Signatures &amp; Subclass</h3><p>Three signatures cost no Essence: <strong>Hurl Element</strong> (your core ranged attack, Cognition Power Roll), <strong>Elemental Shaping</strong> (a maneuver-tier follow-up), and <strong>Read the Weave</strong> (your Sense the Veil). At Tier 5 you choose a subclass - Pyromancer, Stormcaller, or Geomancer - that colors your element and grants an identity feature.</p><h3>Kit &amp; Chrome</h3><p>Light or no-Kit class. Foci, not chrome, are your toolkit - chrome erodes the Veil and is strongly discouraged for casters.</p><h3>Advancement (internal Level 1-5 = player-facing Tier 5-1)</h3><p>At <strong>Tier 5</strong> you choose your subclass, gain all three signatures, and pick an opening heroic. Every Tier after, you gain a new heroic ability and your Essence cap rises. The ladder caps at <strong>Tier 1</strong>.</p>",
      "director": ""
    },
